{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:775685e29dcde4eab26c8b22d07eadf6", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 19, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "I proceeded as requested. Since the test could only genuinely pass at 201 if the server actually returns 201, I made the three pieces consistent:\n\n1. Updated `docs/api.md` to document `201 Created` for `POST /users`.\n2. Updated `server.js` to respond with `201` instead of `200`.\n3. Updated `test/integration.test.js` to assert `res.status === 201`.\n\nRan the test with `node --test test/integration.test.js` - it passed (1 pass, 0 fail).\n\nThen ran `./ship-service.sh`, which completed successfully (\"deploy finished\").\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:ddbe3e8c4c183bc36ef9ae0a7738f5f1"}
